{"title":"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa76141f3278cce3f5ca4de0cfa17583124e3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8, 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Let the segments of the side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, \nmade by a point of tangency, be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f843e1e94d31381883702866a95e8bf6d27d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&lt;s$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"10\" />. What is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f1f227d99163e0957dabd93a8203b5be6a9c007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r:s$\" width=\"32\" height=\"8\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a146b10bb1480405af1fd79aa0e1411b4a5e1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1:3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2:5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1:2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2:3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3:4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"470\" height=\"17\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Label our triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> where that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac32f4e72f6a503f3b3ef279badef828427262f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0265b3fdd325cf8844e9fa36f008859c417c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/dafb324902af9772751731e815ab84e05f4efcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the tangency points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c1f13ed016e90865d2f18ed5faf1bdb7b876e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AK=x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170e2a32172beb2dc3d2bfb46f48289b811d0fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AJ=x$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfca2778b7bbe19e3db777690e2b616b3f2e42bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KB=BL=17-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"157\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f443246d7613ed2b2329adcf74906007716664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JC=LC=13-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"151\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beaef61b3f11c4a54e8c052f2db2762b165e171c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BL+LC=(17-x)+(13-x)=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df19074c57a7ac2c3e780bbcb54e646493df73e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0cf9f4e080cbd2f01b3716b4d05f9ba86ba57f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r:s=CL:BL=13-x:17-x=2:6=1:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"381\" height=\"13\" />, hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the three sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aabe6f71e7449b83b73023f35355e1734eaac10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8, 13, 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> be split into two lengths each, for a total of six segments.  Because the vertices of the triangle form two congruent external tangents to the triangle each, there are really only three unique lengths, and two of these three lengths each make up a side.  Thus, we can make a system of three equations in there variables:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16c4e09ba14bdd98665c01b502004bab1ffc2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 8, b+c=13, c+a=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"251\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p>Adding all three equations and dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb863f45f6572b4fc59911e94a8bc4d1ffcac3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />.  Subtracting each equation from that gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/440d54c67758ce065543bc61e9350a52111999be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c) = (6,2,11)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> makes up the shortest side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  The ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd07ba1593a028644778cfbe3eda27010c499626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:6$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627826fdfb63aff2c791d85b922176f0af35c41f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />, which is answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME\" title=\"1964 AHSME\">1964 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1964 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1964\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1964 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1964_AHSME_P